      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T09:32:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A record with more than one vendor-defined descriptor looks like it keeps only the first. libpldm++ holds `recordDescriptors` in a `std::map` keyed on the descriptor type, and every vendor-defined descriptor shares `PLDM_FWUP_VENDOR_DEFINED`, so the second `emplace()` is a no-op — which is also why `Descriptors` is a `std::multimap` on this side.\n\nWith a package built by `pldm_fwup_pkg_creator.py` from one record holding a UUID plus two vendor-defined descriptors (`TitleA` and `TitleB`):\n\n- master: 3 descriptors, both vendor-defined ones present\n- this patch: 2 descriptors, only `TitleA`\n\nlibpldm++ has already declared `PackageParser::parse` stable, and changing the container type would not be an append, so it would trip the ABI check. I should have caught this during the libpldm++ review. Nothing for this change to do — noting it while libpldm++ still has no other consumers.",
      "revId": "24adc64c379c3bb9110a9380ef7994520044a192",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
